<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What Tauri's bundler adds to the Info.plist it writes for the Mac (bundle.macOS.infoPlist in
  tauri.conf.json): the documents Redlines opens and edits, which Finder's Open With offers it for
  (src/document_types.rs). The file isn't named Info.plist, so that only the bundle has it, and not
  the program that `tauri dev` runs.

  - Markdown, by its types, at the rank of an app that opens it: net.daringfireball.markdown, which
    `.md` files have and Redlines can be made the default app for (Preferences › General), and
    public.markdown, which other apps declare (Word does, as a type that conforms to nothing), so
    that Open With offers Redlines for a file typed that way too (#347).
  - R Markdown and Quarto, by their extensions, which macOS has no type for, and plain text, by
    .txt alone, each at the rank of an alternative: Redlines is offered for those files and takes
    none of them, even where no other app owns them, since people who write R Markdown or Quarto
    have an editor of their choice. Plain text's type would offer Redlines for every kind of text
    that is plain text to macOS, such as source code, which Redlines doesn't open.

  The import says what Markdown is, for a macOS that doesn't know it. public.markdown is for
  others to declare, so the bundle only claims it, and imports no more than the one type.

  The usage descriptions are what macOS's question says when it asks whether Redlines may read a
  folder it protects (Privacy & Security › Files and Folders). It asks for Redlines, whatever
  program reads, when a person lets an agent read their home folder (Preferences › Agents), since
  an agent that Redlines starts is counted as Redlines' own. Without them the question says only
  that Redlines would like to access files in the folder.

  Every key here replaces Tauri's own of that name, so the file holds no other.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>CFBundleDocumentTypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Markdown Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Default</string>
      <key>LSItemContentTypes</key>
      <array>
        <string>net.daringfireball.markdown</string>
        <string>public.markdown</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>R Markdown Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>Rmd</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Quarto Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>qmd</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>CFBundleTypeName</key>
      <string>Plain Text Document</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
      <string>Editor</string>
      <key>LSHandlerRank</key>
      <string>Alternate</string>
      <key>CFBundleTypeExtensions</key>
      <array>
        <string>txt</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>UTImportedTypeDeclarations</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
      <string>net.daringfireball.markdown</string>
      <key>UTTypeDescription</key>
      <string>Markdown</string>
      <key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
      <array>
        <string>public.plain-text</string>
      </array>
      <key>UTTypeTagSpecification</key>
      <dict>
        <key>public.filename-extension</key>
        <array>
          <string>md</string>
          <string>markdown</string>
        </array>
        <key>public.mime-type</key>
        <array>
          <string>text/markdown</string>
        </array>
      </dict>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>NSDesktopFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSDownloadsFolderUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSFileProviderDomainUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSNetworkVolumesUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
  <key>NSRemovableVolumesUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Redlines opens and saves your documents here. If you let an agent such as Claude or Codex read your home folder, it reads other files here through Redlines, and changes only the document.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
